+# BLUE CURRENT V49.20.0 — GO-LIVE COMMAND
+
+V49.16–V49.20 adds the final human-controlled command layer before and after production cutover.
+
+## Final pre-cutover checks
+
+Each location with a prepared deployment package is re-evaluated for:
+
+1. Deployment package prepared.
+2. Human go-live authorization still present.
+3. Technical readiness complete or explicitly overridden at authorization.
+4. Deployment owner assigned.
+5. Rollback owner assigned.
+6. Launch window defined.
+7. Production cutover has not already been recorded successful.
+
+Open final checks require a documented executive override before manual cutover can be authorized.
+
+## Manual cutover execution authorization
+
+Adds:
+
+`POST /api/go-live-command/locations/:locationId/authorize-execution`
+
+Authorization records:
+
+- deployment package
+- location / rollout wave
+- deployment operator
+- rollback operator
+- launch window
+- authenticated authorizer
+- final pre-cutover snapshot
+- override status and reason
+- note
+
+The resulting state is:
+
+- `status: AUTHORIZED_FOR_MANUAL_CUTOVER`
+- `deploymentExecutionState: AUTHORIZED_NOT_EXECUTED`
+- `productionCutoverState: NOT_PERFORMED`
+
+Authorization does not run commands, deploy infrastructure, modify connectors, or perform production cutover.
+
+## Human-recorded cutover result
+
+Adds:
+
+`POST /api/go-live-command/locations/:locationId/record-result`
+
+Supported results:
+
+- `CUTOVER_SUCCEEDED`
+- `CUTOVER_FAILED`
+- `ROLLED_BACK`
+
+Results can only be recorded after manual execution authorization.
+
+A successful cutover result requires every post-cutover health check to be explicitly confirmed:
+
+- API healthy
+- authentication healthy
+- reservation integrity
+- floor integrity
+- kitchen integrity
+- workforce integrity
+
+A failed result requires a launch incident description.
+
+A rollback requires a rollback operator.
+
+Each result explicitly records:
+
+- `resultSource: HUMAN_RECORDED`
+- `systemExecutionClaim: false`
+
+Blue Current records what a human deployment operator reports. It does not claim to have executed the deployment.
+
+## Launch incident state
+
+Failed cutover records preserve the launch incident narrative for subsequent stabilization and incident-command workflows.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- `explicitExecutionAuthorizationRequired: true`
+- `adminExecutionAuthorizationRequired: true`
+- `authorizationDoesNotExecuteDeployment: true`
+- `resultRecordingIsManual: true`
+- `automatedCutover: false`
+- `autonomousProductionDeployment: false`
+- `rollbackMustBeHumanDirected: true`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The untouched Chefs runtime has not executed the rollout, technical authorization, and deployment-package chain.
+
+V49.20 therefore correctly reports:
+
+- status: `deployment-package-required`
+- locations in Go-Live Command: 0
+- autonomous production deployment: false
+
+The current demo owner account does not hold the required `admin` permission. Its attempts to authorize manual cutover and record a cutover result both correctly return HTTP 403.
+
+## Validation
+
+- V49.20 focused Go-Live Command lifecycle PASS
+- final pre-cutover checks PASS
+- manual cutover authorization PASS
+- authorization remains NOT_EXECUTED PASS
+- incomplete health confirmation blocks success PASS
+- human-recorded successful cutover path PASS
+- post-cutover health verification PASS
+- system execution claim remains false PASS
+- V49.15 deployment-package regression PASS
+- authenticated Go-Live Command GET PASS
+- admin-only execution authorization boundary PASS
+- admin-only result-recording boundary PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 893 JavaScript files
+- 754 client scripts
+- 5,622 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V49.21–V49.25 should build Launch Stabilization:
+- post-launch observation window
+- location health timeline
+- launch incidents / degradations
+- rollback recommendation state
+- adoption/readiness after launch
+- first-service verification
+- stabilization exit criteria
+- human declaration of STABLE / EXTEND / ROLLBACK
+- no autonomous rollback
